<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9843]  IgniteClientReconnectCacheQueriesFailoverTest fails: grid loses type meta without losing data</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9843</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=2052100&amp;amp;#testNameId6624729862379349247&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=2052100&amp;amp;#testNameId6624729862379349247&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
org.apache.ignite.IgniteCheckedException: Cannot find metadata &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; object with compact footer: -1058754203
Caused by: org.apache.ignite.binary.BinaryObjectException: Cannot find metadata &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; object with compact footer: -1058754203
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I was thinking that it can be fixed by adding ignite.binary().type(Person.class) before doing query, but it appears to be not the case.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
